  "difficulty_level": "H3",
  "difficulty_reason": "After standard Peano/cyclic-order facts and the named universal-tree-group prerequisites are supplied, the original local core reconstructs the circle/cut-point incidence tree and a topology subbasis, extends compatible legal cyclic colorings over the entire biregular tree, and lifts its separation-preserving automorphisms through circle fibers and ends. It identifies exactly the homeomorphism group and then proves continuity of this identification by recognizing a fixed circle from three complementary branches. This global topological-group reconstruction for finite n>=3 is substantially beyond qualification-level tree automorphisms or compact-space pointwise maps; no count is assigned to the already-known basilica case n=2 or to the unselected infinite-order case.",
